            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for remains, then the Telugu for to unearth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: శాసనం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "శాసనం — śāsanaṁ — \"an inscription; an edict\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ రాతి మీద ఒక పాత శాసనం ఉంది. ā rāti mīda oka pāta śāsanaṁ undi. There is an old inscription on that stone."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kings carved their orders and gifts on stone and copper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "శాసనం (śāsanaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit śāsana, \"a command; a royal edict\" (CDIAL 12420)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
