              "text": "యుగం — yugaṁ — \"an era; an age\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇది కంప్యూటర్ల యుగం. idi kampyūṭarla yugaṁ. This is the age of computers."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: యుగాలు, yugālu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The old stories count time in యుగాలు, ages; today the word also names an era of history."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "యుగం (yugaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit yuga (CDIAL 10482), whose first sense is \"a yoke\"; it came to mean an age of the world."
